invariant: INV-13
file: src/tls_write_rules.h
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_fail_out takes close_notify as an error alert, so a caller
  that passes 0 fails the session and writes a close_notify it did not
  mean. RFC 9846 §6.1 makes it a closure alert, which ch_close_out writes.
  bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires CH_EINVAL and nothing written for
  it.

--- old
    static const uint8_t error_alerts[] = {
        10,  // unexpected_message
--- new
    static const uint8_t error_alerts[] = {
        0,   // close_notify
        10,  // unexpected_message
